 graph G."}, {"y0": 0.6671511632277722, "y1": 0.6818181817713624, "x0": 0.23308271431514668, "x1": 0.5714285678277103, "t": "Which of the following options is/are correct?"}, {"y0": 0.7122093025929972, "y1": 0.7281976744709564, "x0": 0.1898496240049352, "x1": 0.22180451189732048, "t": "(A)"}, {"y0": 0.7136627911251441, "y1": 0.7267441856674913, "x0": 0.22556391315661364, "x1": 0.6052631418559181, "t": "| Root of T can never be an articulation point in G."}, {"y0": 0.7601744188720668, "y1": 0.7761627907500261, "x0": 0.19172932413337868, "x1": 0.22180451097940324, "t": "(B)"}, {"y0": 0.7616279069498612, "y1": 0.7733333332526843, "x0": 0.23308272494952942, "x1": 0.8101503721839289, "t": "Root of T is an articulation point in G if and only if it has 2 or more children."}, {"y0": 0.8095930236928884, "y1": 0.8241279069030417, "x0": 0.18984962495104785, "x1": 0.21992481179707243, "t": "(C)"}, {"y0": 0.8095930236832837, "y1": 0.8226744182256309, "x0": 0.23496241896426412, "x1": 0.5695488703841064, "t": "A leaf of T can be an articulation point in G."}, {"y0": 0.8575581399719583, "y1": 0.8720930231821116, "x0": 0.18984962495104785, "x1": 0.21992481179707243, "t": "(D)"}, {"y0": 0.8575581398836228, "y1": 0.8709090907604946, "x0": 0.23496241281453822, "x1": 0.8364661736516269, "t": "If u is an articulation point in G such that a is an ancestor of u in T and y is a"}, {"y0": 0.8733333334361382, "y1": 0.8866666667694716, "x0": 0.23496241253978786, "x1": 0.7857142929583322, "t": "descendent of u in T, then all paths from x to y in G must pass through u."}, {"y0": 0.9460606063120072, "y1": 0.9607558137344371, "x0": 0.15225563874059372, "x1": 0.3966165356015116, "t": "CS, Set-1 - Copyright \u00a9 GATE 2021"}, {"y0": 0.9461047426870524, "y1": 0.9594185135592262, "x0": 0.7537325871255258, "x1": 0.8477711707674151, "t": "Page 33 of 40"}]